 "answer": {
  "answer": "Four of the five cases the brief asked for were confirmed, each on a different scene. All four delay the key car by 1 s and slow it to 0.5x or 0.75x. The ego's hand-off speed differs between them: 1.4x on 096988dd and 0e899dd3, 1.2x on 19f339ba and 0.8x on 1c45ce3a. The ranges put each of the four above 0.5, but each rests on only a few repeats, so the true rates are only loosely known. Only two of the four are clearly the policy's fault: on 096988dd and 19f339ba the policy steered left, against a straight route, into a car in the next lane (not the retimed car). The other two may not be: on 0e899dd3 the policy took over half a second before a rear-end crash it had little room to avoid, and on 1c45ce3a a replayed car cut in from behind in most runs. No failure was flagged as a possible simulator artifact. The best fifth candidate (09a95ffa, car +0.5 s at 0.75x, ego 1.4x) failed every time but has too few runs to confirm.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "Confirmed on 096988dd with the car delayed 1 s at 0.5x speed and the ego at 1.4x. In every failure the policy bent its path left on a straight highway, against a STRAIGHT then RIGHT route, and hit a car alongside in the left lane. That car was not the retimed one. The policy was at fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S14"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Confirmed on 19f339ba with the car delayed 1 s at 0.5x speed and the ego at 1.2x. With no close lead, the policy braked hard for no visible reason, drifted left and hit a car passing in the left lane. The policy was at fault in every failure.",
    "settings": [
     "S41"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Confirmed on 0e899dd3 with the car delayed 1 s at 0.75x speed and the ego at 1.4x. These are rear-end hits on the slowed lead pickup. At hand-off the gap was already only about 5.7 m and closing, and the crash came 0.5 s later. Triage called the fault unclear in most runs, so this case mostly reflects the state the policy inherited, not its own driving.",
    "settings": [
     "S25"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Confirmed on 1c45ce3a with the car delayed 1 s at 0.5x speed and the ego slowed to 0.8x. The ego lagged behind the recording, and a replayed car coming from behind in the right lane met its front-right corner. Triage blamed the policy's rightward drift in only one run and called the others unclear, mostly the other car cutting in. Neighbouring ego speeds on this scene did not fail in their single runs.",
